From abd000972c2e53543c4fc31b03d2e298d971ff3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:25:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the series' floating elements keep to the
 conversation's column
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.30, ask 50 (operator, 2026-11-13): "the width of every
element must follow the agent panel's maximum".

Upstream caps the entries, the activity bar and the composer at
`agent.max_content_width` (850 px by default, while
`agent.limit_content_width` is on) and centres them. Of the series' own
elements only 0087 read that setting. On a panel wider than the column the
rest spanned the whole agent area while the messages around them stayed in
the middle: the pinned user message (0102: `.absolute().left_2().right_2()`
against the panel), the question card and its minimized bar (0027, 0082:
`.w_full()`), the tasks card's bottom bar (0092), the floating tasks card in
its corner and its eye preview (0037, 0094: the frame was the free area of
the whole panel), and the floating navigation controls (0026: `right_4` of
the panel).

What changes. `thread_view/content_column.rs` holds one helper,
`content_column`, which is upstream's own `centered_container` from
`render_entries` (h_flex w_full justify_center around a div max_w(max) w_full),
so the series and upstream cannot disagree about where the column is. The
pinned message and the navigation controls keep their absolute layer over
the conversation and put their content in the column inside it; the
controls sit at the column's right edge (`justify_end`), and `right_4`
still clears the scrollbar for a column as wide as the panel. The question
card, its bar and the docked tasks bar go through the same helper in the
thread's bottom slots. The floating tasks card is placed in a free area
measured at prepaint, so it gets a pure function instead,
`tasks_card::within_content_column`, applied to that area in
`AgentPanel::render_tasks_card`: the card's corner becomes the column's
corner, and a preview that widens to its frame (0094) widens to the column.
With `limit_content_width` off there is no maximum and every element is as
wide as before -- tested, so the fix cannot invent a width of its own.

Two debug selectors are added for the tests: `pinned-elicitations` and
`thread-floating-navigation`.

Tests, each seen failing first with the helper reduced to a pass-through
and the free area unclamped (6 failed, the 3 that must hold either way
passed): tasks_card::content_width (the floating card in all four corners,
the docked bar, the corner without a maximum, two unit tests of
within_content_column) and thread_view::tests::content_width_tests (the
pinned message, the navigation controls, the question card and its bar,
the bar without a maximum). Neighbours green: placement, dock_bottom,
question_card, pinned_message, tasks_card -- 244 tests.

